Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:23:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 437/437] AI chat: History: go back to an earlier conversation
 and go on with it

"New conversation" pressed by mistake threw the conversation away (feedback 2026-11-26). The
bridge now reports each conversation's session id and can resume one; the panel keeps the last 30
conversations (title = the first request, time, what was shown) in <user data>/ai/chats, saved
after every answer and on quit. History lists them; picking one shows it again and the AI goes on
from it (Claude keeps the conversation itself). Checked with the AI: a password told in one
conversation was unknown in a new one and remembered again after going back through History.
